Fun and creepy. Get some friends to play with (at least for the campaign) as you'll need it. The atmosphere is great, the first time i played it (solo) it scared the sh*t out of me and i went and got a friend to play with me. You get used to it but some of it can give you the chills. Soundtrack is amazing (in my opinion). It's got that theme song that you'll find yourself humming at random times. The community is shrinking but there are still plenty of people willing to play it.
Price;
too expensive for how short it is. Not saying it is a short game, but it doesn't take more than 15 hours to finish the campaign on Marksman difficulty. I got this for the Steam Winter Sale 2016 for 9 dollars. it is not worth the full 45 unless you really think you are going to play the hell out of it. Wait for a sale as it is much less painful to shell out 9 dollars for this than 45.

It's full of quicktime events;
it's unoptimised;
it's a Crytek title (shine over substance);
it's a dead franchise because of a dispute between Crytek/Microsoft;
it's very short (~5 hours campaign);
it's a poor iteration of the Arkham clichés (Shadow of Mordor, Mad Max, Hand of Fate style of combat) with minimal telegraphing and enemies attacking at the same time (with no dual-block/parry);
it's without a singular memorable character.
But I enjoyed it? I probably shouldn't, it doesn't do much to expand gamer's experiences, but I did enjoy it.
Soft recommendation if you got it for free / in the Humble Monthly / it's ever on sale for the price of a hot meal. I think there is fun to be had in this game, but nothing groundbreaking. It's got some meaty muscular manmen and voluptuous vixens if that's your thing.

